{"evidence":[{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Karen Rollins Jackson (born November 21, 1965) is the current Virginia Secretary of Technology, having been appointed in 2014 by Governor Terry McAuliffe.","title":"Karen Jackson"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" She previously served from 2009 to 2014 as Deputy Secretary of Technology under Governors Tim Kaine and Bob McDonnell.","title":"Karen Jackson"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" Jackson was born in Newport News, Virginia and was raised in Poquoson.","title":"Karen Jackson"},{"sentence_id":3,"text":" She attended Christopher Newport University, graduating in 1987, and received a Master in Business Administration degree from the College of William & Mary.","title":"Karen Jackson"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"The Secretary of Technology is a member of the Virginia Governor's Cabinet.","title":"Virginia Secretary of Technology"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" The office is currently held by Karen Jackson.","title":"Virginia Secretary of Technology"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" The Secretary oversees the Virginia Information Technologies Agency and Virginia Center for Innovative Technology.","title":"Virginia Secretary of Technology"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Donald Earl Jackson (born June 23, 1930) is a former Canadian politician, who represented the electoral district of Timiskaming in the Legislative Assembly of Ontario from 1967 to 1971.","title":"Donald Jackson (Canadian politician)"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" He was a member of the Ontario New Democratic Party.","title":"Donald Jackson (Canadian politician)"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" After winning in the general election, in 1967, Jackson served one term, losing to the PC candidate Ed Havrot.","title":"Donald Jackson (Canadian politician)"},{"sentence_id":3,"text":" As an opposition member, Jackson served on a variety of Standing Committees, particularly those, like the Standing Committee on Natural Resources, Wildlife and Mining, with particular significance to his riding in northern Ontario.","title":"Donald Jackson (Canadian politician)"},{"sentence_id":4,"text":" He was born in Shannonville, Ontario.","title":"Donald Jackson (Canadian politician)"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Luther Hartwell Hodges Jr. (born November 19, 1936) is a retired American politician and banker.","title":"Luther H. Hodges Jr."},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" He was the first United States Deputy Secretary of Commerce (1980–81), appointed under Jimmy Carter.","title":"Luther H. Hodges Jr."},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" Previously Under Secretary of Commerce, he had been tapped to replace Juanita M. Kreps as Secretary of Commerce, but, after a spell as Acting Secretary, the job went to Philip Klutznick, and the new Deputy Secretary position was created for him.","title":"Luther H. Hodges Jr."},{"sentence_id":3,"text":" Hodges' father, Luther H. Hodges Sr., had been Secretary of Commerce under John F. Kennedy and Lyndon B. Johnson between 1961 and 1965, and was also the 64th governor of North Carolina.","title":"Luther H. Hodges Jr."},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Rebecca M. Blank (born September 19, 1955) is the current chancellor of the University of Wisconsin-Madison and former Acting United States Secretary of Commerce.","title":"Rebecca Blank"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" Blank was serving as United States Deputy Secretary of Commerce when she was named to lead the United States Department of Commerce as Acting Secretary on June 11, 2012 upon the request of Secretary of Commerce John Bryson, who took a medical leave of absence, and subsequently resigned as Secretary.","title":"Rebecca Blank"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" She had held the role of Deputy Secretary since October 21, 2011.","title":"Rebecca Blank"},{"sentence_id":3,"text":" Blank was previously the Acting Secretary from July 2011 until October 2011, following the appointment of Gary Locke as United States Ambassador to China.","title":"Rebecca Blank"},{"sentence_id":4,"text":" A native of Missouri, Blank is a "summa cum laude" graduate in economics from the University of Minnesota and holds a Ph.D. in economics from the Massachusetts Institute of Technology.","title":"Rebecca Blank"},{"sentence_id":5,"text":" On March 18, 2013, she was recommended for the position of Chancellor at the University of Wisconsin–Madison.","title":"Rebecca Blank"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Timothy Michael Kaine ( , born February 26, 1958) is an American attorney and politician who is the junior United States Senator from Virginia.","title":"Tim Kaine"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" A Democrat, Kaine was elected to the Senate in 2012 and was the nominee of his party for Vice President of the United States in the 2016 election.","title":"Tim Kaine"}],"peer_messages":["Unverified peer answer: Democratic
